{
 "id": "2026-10-25-e-to-the-x",
 "topic": "why e^x is its own derivative",
 "subject": "math",
 "hook_type": "curiosity jump",
 "caption": "Slide along the graph of eˣ and the slope of the tangent always equals the height. Growth proportional to size: that's what makes e special, and why it runs populations, interest and radioactive decay.\n\nShare this with someone learning calculus.\n\n#calculus #math #mathematics #derivatives #stem #engineering #physics #learnmath",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "There's a function whose slope is always exactly its height.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "Here's $e^x$. Pick any point on its graph.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "axes",
     "name": "ax",
     "x": [
      -2.5,
      2.2,
      1
     ],
     "y": [
      0,
      8,
      2
     ],
     "size": [
      7.4,
      6.4
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      0.2
     ],
     "labels": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "graph",
     "name": "g",
     "on": "ax",
     "fn": "exp(x)",
     "x": [
      -2.5,
      2.05
     ],
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "make": "tracker",
     "name": "t",
     "value": -1.0
    },
    {
     "make": "dot",
     "name": "p",
     "follow": "g",
     "x": "t",
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The tangent line there measures how fast the function is growing at that moment.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tangent",
     "name": "tan",
     "graph": "g",
     "x": "t",
     "length": 3.2,
     "color": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "make": "readout",
     "name": "slope",
     "tracker": "t",
     "fn": "exp(x)",
     "label": "\\text{slope} =",
     "at": [
      0,
      5.5
     ],
     "color": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "make": "readout",
     "name": "height",
     "tracker": "t",
     "fn": "exp(x)",
     "label": "\\text{height} =",
     "at": [
      0,
      4.6
     ],
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Now slide the point along, and keep an eye on both numbers.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "whoosh"
    },
    {
     "slide": "t",
     "to": 1.6,
     "time": 3.0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "They never disagree. At every point, the slope equals the height.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "indicate": [
      "slope",
      "height"
     ]
    },
    {
     "slide": "t",
     "to": 0.3,
     "time": 1.6
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In symbols: the derivative of $e^x$ is just $e^x$ again.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "eq",
     "tex": [
      "\\frac{d}{dx}",
      "e^x",
      "=",
      "e^x"
     ],
     "size": 110,
     "at": [
      0,
      2.4
     ],
     "colors": {
      "1": "blue",
      "3": "blue"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx",
     "around": "eq"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Call the function $y$, and it says something physical: the rate of growth is proportional to the amount.",
   "do": [
    {
     "hide": "bx",
     "time": 0.3
    },
    {
     "morph": "eq",
     "into": {
      "make": "tex",
      "tex": [
       "\\frac{dy}{dx}",
       "=",
       "y"
      ],
      "size": 120,
      "colors": {
       "0": "yellow",
       "2": "blue"
      },
      "at": [
       0,
       2.4
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "brace",
     "name": "b1",
     "of": "eq",
     "side": "down",
     "text": "rate = amount"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "That one rule runs populations, compound interest and radioactive decay.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "text",
     "name": "l1",
     "text": "populations",
     "size": 60,
     "color": "teal",
     "at": [
      0,
      -0.6
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "text",
     "name": "l2",
     "text": "compound interest",
     "size": 60,
     "color": "yellow",
     "next_to": "l1",
     "buff": 0.35
    },
    {
     "make": "text",
     "name": "l3",
     "text": "radioactive decay",
     "size": 60,
     "color": "brown",
     "next_to": "l2",
     "buff": 0.35
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Whenever change feeds on itself, $e$ is hiding nearby.",
   "do": [
    {
     "flash": "eq"
    },
    {
     "indicate": "eq",
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
